      "guide": "Complete the final mission for Tyrone. His questline is Jason-only and marks automatically after Chapter 3's Here, Kitty Kitty. Destroy the Synthetic Labs (purple markers, quest Take Out Kitty Litter), then Tyrone's second quest Spin On This shuts the labs down. All of it stays available after the story.",
      "steps": ["Play as Jason after Chapter 3's Here, Kitty Kitty", "Destroy the Synthetic Labs (Take Out Kitty Litter)", "Finish Tyrone's second quest, Spin On This"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 28, "name": "Positive Mental Attitude", "description": "Meditate at every spot across Leonida.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "collectibles", "stage": 1, "chapter": "Ch 1 → anytime", "difficulty": 2, "time": "2–4 h", "missable": true, "unconfirmed": true,
      "guide": "Meditate at every spot across Leonida — 18 meditation spots at 10 locations. Meditating with both Jason and Lucia at a spot counts double (+2), and the last spot needs both characters together (after Coffee Break in Chapter 2). Track it under Progress > Collections > Exploration > Meditations. MISSABLE: the first meditation, on the balcony of Jason's house, only happens in Chapter 1 — after Down to Earth, Lucia mentions meditating in the kitchen in the morning, walks to the balcony, and you follow and accept. It adds +1 to the counter but is not marked as a spot, and it is NOT yet confirmed whether the trophy strictly needs it — do it anyway and keep a Chapter 1 save until the trophy pops. For 100% you only need 15 of 18.",
      "target": { "label": "meditation spots", "total": 18 },
      "steps": ["Ch 1 only: after Down to Earth, talk to Lucia in the kitchen", "Follow her to the balcony and accept the meditation", "Keep a manual Chapter 1 save until this trophy pops", "Meditate at all 18 spots — bring your partner (+2 each)", "Last spot needs both characters (after Coffee Break)"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5],
      "missable_note": "End of Chapter 1. Lucia's balcony meditation at Jason's house is offered once and never returns. Not yet confirmed whether the trophy needs it — do it anyway and keep a Chapter 1 save.",
      "unconfirmed_note": "Not yet confirmed whether the Chapter 1 balcony meditation is strictly required for the trophy — PowerPyx says it is still undergoing confirmation." },
    { "id": 29, "name": "Fair Game", "description": "Hunt a unique animal for Bret.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": true, "kind": "strands", "stage": 3, "chapter": "Ch 2+", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 2+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": true,
      "guide": "Hunt a unique animal for Bret. Bret Vogel's questline marks automatically after Chapter 2's Coffee Break — as Jason you get a text marking Veteran Hunted in Lummox County (Jason-only). He gives you the Killtelligence SM-69 hunting rifle (retrieve it from any Ammu-Nation weapon locker) and marks hunting spots; bring him the animals he requests. A clean head or heart shot keeps the carcass pristine and pays more. It is still being confirmed which animal exactly unlocks this — the questline has 15 Target Decks, all needed for 100%, so work it through and it should land.",
      "steps": ["After Coffee Break, wait for Bret's text as Jason", "Meet Bret (Veteran Hunted, Lummox County)", "Hunt the animals he requests and bring them to him", "Work through all 15 Target Decks"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5],
      "unconfirmed_note": "Not yet confirmed which animal exactly unlocks this trophy — PowerPyx says it is still undergoing confirmation." },
    { "id": 30, "name": "Don't Touch My Deck", "description": "Complete 3 Collectible Card sets.", "grade": "silver", "hidden": false, "kind": "collectibles", "stage": 5, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 2, "time": "3–5 h", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "card sets", "total": 3 },
      "guide": "Complete 3 Collectible Card sets. There are 18 card set locations in total — collect the cards around Leonida and finish any 3 full sets. Cards also count toward the 100% checklist in part, so collect as you go rather than saving them all for the end.",
      "steps": ["Find collectible cards around Leonida (18 set locations)", "Complete any 3 full sets", "Cards also count toward the 100% checklist"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 31, "name": "You WAiNKer!", "description": "WAiNK It at 100 locations.", "grade": "silver", "hidden": false, "kind": "collectibles", "stage": 5, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 1, "time": "3–5 h", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "WAiNK scans", "total": 100 },
      "guide": "WAiNK It at 100 locations. Hold up on the D-pad then R1 to scan landmarks, curiosities and sculptures — 31 landmarks, 35 curiosities, 23 sculptures, plus No Flusher tags; more than 100 exist, so scan any 100. Scanning vehicles with WAiNK also counts toward Whip It Good, so scan everything you pass.",
      "steps": ["Hold up on the D-pad, then R1 to scan", "Scan landmarks, curiosities and sculptures as you travel", "Any 100 scans count — there are more than 100 to find"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 32, "name": "One Last Thing", "description": "Complete 50 Challenges.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "activities", "stage": 4, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Across the run", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "challenges", "total": 50 },
      "guide": "Complete 50 Challenges. 80 exist and 100% needs 70, so this pops on the way to the platinum. Track them under Progress > Challenges; many complete naturally while you play. Save the easiest ones for last, then pick the quickest of what remains.",
      "steps": ["Open Progress > Challenges to see them all", "Let most complete naturally while chasing other trophies", "Pick the easiest remaining challenges to reach 50 (70 for 100%)"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 33, "name": "Hot Together", "description": "Lose a 4 star Wanted Level with your partner and escape the heat.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 2+", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 2+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Lose a 4-star Wanted Level with your partner and escape the heat. Earliest after Coffee Break (Chapter 2), when you can call your partner (hold right on the D-pad, press Triangle). Cause carnage to 4 stars, then escape the red heat zone — the trophy pops after leaving the heat zone, not the flashing search area. Easy escape: the train tunnel north of Ambrosia in Kelly County, where cops struggle on the tracks and the helicopter cannot see you. It also pops automatically during the Chapter 4 vault robberies, which always give 4 stars.",
      "steps": ["After Coffee Break, call your partner", "Build a 4-star wanted level", "Escape the red heat zone — try the train tunnel north of Ambrosia", "Or let it pop automatically during the Chapter 4 bank vaults"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 34, "name": "Retail Therapy", "description": "Rob 3 shops back-to-back with your partner without losing your Wanted Level.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 2+", "difficulty": 3, "time": "Ch 2+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Rob 3 shops back-to-back with your partner without losing your Wanted Level. Call your partner, then hit 3 robbery targets (green icons) while the police chase you the whole time — keep the flashing wanted level alive, not the red heat level. The pop is delayed about 30 seconds after the third shop; if it does not pop, hit a 4th. A good spot is the 3 jewelry stores in north Vice City (after Yasmani's Jewelry Jobs). Wear an armored vest and carry Sticky Bombs and healing.",
      "steps": ["Call your partner", "Rob 3 shops in a row while the police chase you", "Keep the flashing wanted level alive between shops", "Wait ~30 seconds after the third shop; hit a 4th if it does not pop"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 35, "name": "Whip It Good", "description": "Discover 100 vehicles.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "collectibles", "stage": 5, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 1, "time": "2–3 h", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "vehicles", "total": 100 },
      "guide": "Discover 100 vehicles. Use the WAiNK app (hold up to open it instantly), look at a vehicle and hold R1 to scan it — scanning is enough, you do not need to drive it. 557 vehicles exist at launch; stand on a busy road and scan traffic. The 100% checklist needs 200 of the 277 base models, so this comes naturally. Check Progress > Vehicles.",
      "steps": ["Open the WAiNK app (hold up on the D-pad)", "Scan vehicles as they pass — no need to drive them", "Any 100 discovered counts (200 of 277 base models for 100%)"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 36, "name": "Gunslinger", "description": "Take down 5 enemies in a single use of Combat Focus.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "misc", "stage": 4, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 3, "time": "Anytime", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "enemies in one Focus", "total": 5 },
      "guide": "Take down 5 enemies in a single use of Combat Focus. Combat Focus is L3+R3 while aiming — time slows and weak spots are highlighted, and it drains the purple focus bar. Buff focus first (food, drinks, washing up at home, Adrenaline to extend it), then line up 5 enemies — gang members at an illegal operation are ideal — and drop them fast with an assault rifle like the Duke 556. It does not seem to work on soldiers, police or civilians. Focus levels up through shooting ranges, golf, pool, fishing and headshots, so it gets easier later.",
      "steps": ["Buff focus: eat, drink, use Adrenaline", "Find 5 grouped gang enemies (an illegal operation works)", "Activate Combat Focus (L3+R3 while aiming) and drop all 5 fast"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 37, "name": "Catch Me If You Can", "description": "Make an unscheduled departure at VCIA.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": true, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 3+", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 3+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Make an unscheduled departure at VCIA. Steal a large passenger plane docked at a boarding bridge — planes parked on the airfield do not count. Easiest at gates E3/E4: drive through a fence, climb the stairs by the bridge, enter the plane, go upstairs to the cockpit, reverse to the runway and take off. Fly about 1 km away and it pops (delayed). Save first — the police come fast.",
      "steps": ["Go to VCIA and drive through a fence to the E3/E4 gates", "Board the plane docked at the bridge and reach the cockpit", "Reverse to the runway, take off and fly ~1 km away"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 38, "name": "Challenging Tank", "description": "Kinda hot in these Rhinos.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": true, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Anytime", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Kinda hot in these Rhinos — steal a military tank. Tanks stand in the south of Mile Zero Air Station, the island at the far south-west of the map in Mariana County. Drive through the gate or use the stunt jump by the south-east entrance, get in and shoot until it pops.",
      "steps": ["Go to Mile Zero Air Station (far south-west island)", "Enter through the gate or the south-east stunt jump", "Get in a tank in the south of the base and fire until it pops"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 39, "name": "Sneakthief", "description": "Rob a jewelry store without being detected.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 3+", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 3+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Rob a jewelry store without being detected. First finish Chapter 3's Yasmani's Jewelry Jobs — it unlocks the Snap Gun and jewelry robberies. Use the Snap Gun on a locked back door (kicking it in sets off the alarm), find the note with the safe code in the back room, open the safe and leave unseen. Richardson Jewelry & Diamonds in Vice City is a good target. If anyone spots you, reload.",
      "steps": ["Finish Chapter 3's Yasmani's Jewelry Jobs to get the Snap Gun", "Pick a jewelry store and use the Snap Gun on its back door", "Find the safe code note, open the safe and leave unseen"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 40, "name": "Maximum Withdrawal", "description": "Rob 5 Bank Vaults and escape.", "grade": "silver", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 4", "difficulty": 3, "time": "Ch 4", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "bank vaults", "total": 5 },
      "guide": "Rob 5 Bank Vaults and escape. It unlocks through the Chapter 4 optional mission That's Where The Money Is… (Wait at the Cafe): tail a security van to a large bank and slip in while the guard has the vault open. Bring your partner — you cannot carry all the bags alone (hold right to hand off a bag). After that, buy van tips from Yasmani for $10,000 a tip (after his Payday Loan jobs). Vaults instantly give a 4-star wanted level — escape on a fast motorcycle, then switch cars to go unrecognized. 8 large bank jobs exist; 100% needs all 8, and one vault can pay up to $205,000.",
      "steps": ["Finish Chapter 4's That's Where The Money Is…", "Tail a security van to a bank and enter while the vault is open", "Bring your partner to carry the bags", "Rob 5 vaults (8 for 100%); buy further van tips from Yasmani"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 41, "name": "A Classic Blitz Play", "description": "Rob an Armored Truck and escape.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 4", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 4", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Rob an Armored Truck and escape. It pops automatically in That's Where The Money Is… — tailing the armored truck to the bank and robbing the vault counts. Earlier method: block an armored truck driving near a bank, plant a Sticky Bomb on its back door and blow it, then escape the red heat radius. Sticky Bombs come from the back of Yasmani's shop after his quests.",
      "steps": ["Play Chapter 4's That's Where The Money Is… — the vault robbery counts", "Or stop an armored truck early: block it, Sticky Bomb its back door", "Escape the red heat radius"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 42, "name": "The Goodtime State", "description": "Explore all of Leonida.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "collectibles", "stage": 5, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 1, "time": "2–3 h", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false,
      "guide": "Explore all of Leonida — fully unfog the whole map. Fastest by plane: fly over every black-fogged area until the entire map is visible. It pairs naturally with the stunt flights for Cunning Stunts.",
      "steps": ["Take a plane and fly over every fogged area", "Watch the map fill in until no black fog remains"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 43, "name": "Pest Control", "description": "Rob an Illegal Operation belonging to each gang.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": false, "kind": "crime", "stage": 6, "chapter": "Ch 2+", "difficulty": 2, "time": "Ch 2+", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": false, "target": { "label": "gangs", "total": 9 },
      "guide": "Rob an Illegal Operation belonging to each gang — 9 gangs, 39 operations in total. One operation per gang is enough for the trophy; the 100% checklist needs all 39. Operations show as yellow icons when you get near them, and many are marked automatically from story progress. Track per gang under Progress > Gangs.",
      "steps": ["Watch for yellow illegal-operation icons on the map", "Rob one operation for each of the 9 gangs", "Track per gang under Progress > Gangs (all 39 for 100%)"],
      "sources": [1, 2, 5] },
    { "id": 44, "name": "In The Beginning…", "description": "Enjoy a cocktail with a view on Ocean Beach.", "grade": "bronze", "hidden": true, "kind": "misc", "stage": 7, "chapter": "Anytime", "difficulty": 1, "time": "Unknown", "missable": false, "unconfirmed": true,
      "guide": "Enjoy a cocktail with a view on Ocean Beach. UNCONFIRMED: PowerPyx lists this trophy as currently unknown — no verified steps exist yet. The description points at a cocktail with an Ocean Beach view, so the bars along Ocean Beach are the natural place to look, but this guide will not invent a fixed spot. Check back — it will be updated the moment players pin it down.",
